WEBVTT

01:21.000 --> 01:22.500
(Alya Sometimes Hides Her Feelings in Russian)

01:31.430 --> 01:33.010
(Episode 8: The Student Council General Meeting)

01:33.100 --> 01:35.220
Is the general meeting's agenda

01:35.300 --> 01:37.650
about the introduction
of a teacher review process

01:37.730 --> 01:39.150
for joining the student council?

01:39.270 --> 01:41.980
They're pinpointing me,
who has a bad impression with teachers,

01:42.060 --> 01:44.060
and launching an all-out attack.

01:44.560 --> 01:46.280
Are you really going to do it?

01:46.370 --> 01:49.410
It won't do you guys any merit, right?

01:49.820 --> 01:51.280
Yes, it will.

01:51.370 --> 01:52.700
If I defeat her,

01:52.780 --> 01:55.320
my reputation
as a presidential candidate will go up.

01:55.790 --> 01:56.710
Besides,

01:56.790 --> 01:59.710
she insulted Kuze and me.

01:59.790 --> 02:01.330
I want her to retract her words

02:01.420 --> 02:02.790
and apologize sincerely,

02:02.880 --> 02:04.000
or I can't take it.

02:04.290 --> 02:05.420
I see.

02:05.890 --> 02:08.640
However, it's not all bad.

02:08.720 --> 02:10.760
We can use this chance
to make an appearance

02:10.840 --> 02:12.510
before the closing ceremony speech.

02:12.760 --> 02:15.300
If you put it that way,
I can't say anything else.

02:15.550 --> 02:16.510
All right.

02:16.600 --> 02:19.020
Let's spread the news today.

02:19.270 --> 02:22.520
President, I'll make the flyers.

02:22.600 --> 02:24.400
Okay, I'm counting on you.

02:25.190 --> 02:27.240
Masachika, Alya,

02:27.320 --> 02:28.610
do your best.

02:28.990 --> 02:30.490
Yes, thank you.

02:30.780 --> 02:31.740
Okay.

02:35.780 --> 02:36.710
Anyway,

02:36.790 --> 02:38.620
based on the current trends,

02:38.710 --> 02:41.210
Taniyama would make this claim.

02:41.580 --> 02:43.000
I see.

02:43.080 --> 02:44.580
Based on this prediction,

02:44.670 --> 02:46.510
how would you refute it?

02:49.590 --> 02:51.590
Well, not bad.

02:51.680 --> 02:54.470
But we still need to organize
the contents of the claim.

02:55.050 --> 02:56.690
Hey, Kuze.

02:57.390 --> 02:58.480
Kuze, are you

02:58.980 --> 03:01.600
on bad terms with Taniyama?

03:02.690 --> 03:03.730
No.

03:03.810 --> 03:05.990
I don't think so.

03:06.400 --> 03:08.610
I think we respect each other a lot.

03:08.700 --> 03:10.360
We got along well in junior high.

03:10.570 --> 03:11.700
I see.

03:11.780 --> 03:15.410
Well then, why did Taniyama do that?

03:15.910 --> 03:17.120
Well, about that.

03:17.660 --> 03:18.830
She probably thinks

03:18.910 --> 03:22.830
that I'm disrupting the election for fun.

03:23.960 --> 03:25.210
Then right from the start,

03:25.290 --> 03:28.010
why did she have this misunderstanding?

03:29.800 --> 03:32.800
I was originally Yuki's partner.

03:33.260 --> 03:36.430
But now, I parted ways with Yuki
who has the highest support

03:37.270 --> 03:39.980
and joined forces with another candidate.

03:40.060 --> 03:42.520
It's only natural
that she thinks I'm messing around.

03:42.770 --> 03:44.020
That's...

03:45.780 --> 03:48.990
So because I paired up with Kuze,

03:49.780 --> 03:51.190
this happened to him?

03:53.190 --> 03:54.820
I'm...

03:55.750 --> 03:57.000
Alya?

03:57.080 --> 03:58.000
What's wrong?

03:59.660 --> 04:02.410
I'll do my best tomorrow.

04:02.950 --> 04:05.340
Yes, you can do it.

04:14.130 --> 04:16.600
Kuzecchi, it's been a while.

04:16.680 --> 04:19.100
I'll be in your care today.

04:19.310 --> 04:21.520
No, that didn't sound right either.

04:22.720 --> 04:25.520
Hey, you're too relaxed, aren't you?

04:25.600 --> 04:30.030
After all, I'm not going to present
in the general meeting.

04:30.110 --> 04:31.900
Of course, I'm relaxed.

04:33.440 --> 04:36.330
Hello, I'm Nonoa Miyamae.

04:36.400 --> 04:39.370
You can say I'm Sayacchi's partner.

04:40.160 --> 04:42.200
I'm Alisa Kujou.

04:42.290 --> 04:44.120
Let's have a meaningful discussion.

04:45.290 --> 04:46.800
How serious of you.

04:46.880 --> 04:49.590
I feel like you'll surprisingly
get along with Sayacchi.

04:51.340 --> 04:53.420
Was that really Taniyama's partner?

04:53.500 --> 04:55.630
Yes, they seem to be childhood friends.

04:56.100 --> 04:58.010
Their personalities
and temperaments differ,

04:58.100 --> 04:59.850
but they're still very close.

04:59.930 --> 05:00.930
I see.

05:01.140 --> 05:03.720
Besides, Miyamae
is at the top of the school hierarchy.

05:04.140 --> 05:06.010
In terms of connections,

05:06.110 --> 05:08.400
she's definitely one
of the best in school.

05:08.480 --> 05:09.610
In the election,

05:09.690 --> 05:11.230
that's indeed a threat.

05:11.570 --> 05:14.020
But don't worry about that now.

05:14.270 --> 05:17.530
Just focus on dealing with Taniyama today.

05:17.780 --> 05:19.780
You're right. I understand.

05:23.120 --> 05:24.780
What do you think about this agenda?

05:24.880 --> 05:26.130
It's hard to say.

05:26.380 --> 05:27.540
Speaking of Taniyama,

05:27.630 --> 05:29.040
she competed with that rich girl

05:29.130 --> 05:30.880
for the junior high presidency, right?

05:30.960 --> 05:32.880
I heard her opponent
is a transfer student?

05:33.090 --> 05:35.890
All I know is that she has good grades.

05:41.890 --> 05:43.390
Can I really do it?

05:44.050 --> 05:47.020
Will I be rejected by everyone again
just like back then?

05:49.150 --> 05:51.190
No, I have to do it.

05:51.560 --> 05:55.020
It's also for the sake of my pair, Kuze.

05:57.120 --> 05:59.120
Can she really express herself well?

05:59.200 --> 06:01.120
Taniyama will win for sure.

06:05.200 --> 06:06.200
...ya.

06:06.540 --> 06:07.460
Alya.

06:08.580 --> 06:09.710
Kuze.

06:10.210 --> 06:11.130
Alya.

06:11.500 --> 06:13.630
Are you really an E cup?

06:15.500 --> 06:16.580
What?

06:16.970 --> 06:18.720
Pervert!

06:18.800 --> 06:20.800
What are you talking about
in this situation?

06:20.890 --> 06:23.720
I can ask you this
precisely because of this situation.

06:24.050 --> 06:25.440
You can't hit me now, right?

06:25.810 --> 06:26.980
Just die already.

06:27.060 --> 06:28.600
Is that how you look at trash?

06:29.770 --> 06:31.520
Do you feel less nervous now?

06:33.270 --> 06:34.310
Alya.

06:34.400 --> 06:36.020
Who is your enemy?

06:36.360 --> 06:37.610
Isn't it Taniyama?

06:38.070 --> 06:38.990
No.

06:39.070 --> 06:40.490
Your enemy

06:40.570 --> 06:42.660
is that ideal,
perfect version of yourself.

06:43.240 --> 06:44.200
So,

06:44.280 --> 06:48.710
just think about how to portray
the coolest version of yourself.

06:49.580 --> 06:50.790
Don't worry.

06:50.870 --> 06:51.920
If anything happens,

06:52.000 --> 06:53.920
I'll take care of everything.

06:56.750 --> 06:58.430
It's time.

06:58.680 --> 07:01.220
We will now begin the general meeting.

07:04.550 --> 07:06.510
The proposers are Sayaka Taniyama

07:06.600 --> 07:08.310
and Nonoa Miyamae.

07:08.690 --> 07:10.520
The opposers are Alisa Kujou

07:10.600 --> 07:12.310
and Masachika Kuze.

07:12.560 --> 07:13.520
The agenda

07:13.600 --> 07:15.640
is the introduction
of a teacher review process

07:15.740 --> 07:17.150
for joining the student council.

07:17.700 --> 07:18.700
Now, proposition,

07:18.780 --> 07:20.110
please present your arguments.

07:20.200 --> 07:21.200
Yes.

07:27.250 --> 07:28.370
Everyone.

07:28.460 --> 07:30.580
Currently, the student council executives

07:30.660 --> 07:34.210
are selected by the president
and vice president.

07:34.660 --> 07:36.510
However, in reality,

07:36.580 --> 07:41.300
it's possible for any student to join
the student council if they want to.

07:41.840 --> 07:42.970
In fact,

07:43.050 --> 07:46.140
- I conducted a survey on
- Does she mean favouritism?

07:46.230 --> 07:47.930
- former council executives.
- I think so.

07:48.020 --> 07:49.180
Seriously?

07:49.270 --> 07:52.600
- She even prepared this kind of data?
- Including the current student council,

07:52.680 --> 07:56.310
- No, it wasn't Taniyama. Was it Miyamae?
- the past three student councils...

07:56.900 --> 07:57.820
I think

07:57.900 --> 08:02.690
The student council should only accept
the top students who have been selected.

08:03.280 --> 08:05.400
Don't you all feel the same way?

08:05.860 --> 08:09.410
Students who usually have
poor grades and bad character,

08:09.500 --> 08:11.660
the moment they become
student council executives,

08:11.750 --> 08:13.620
they'll be above all of you.

08:14.080 --> 08:15.700
Don't you hate that?

08:17.710 --> 08:19.920
She's awesome as I expected.

08:20.010 --> 08:21.710
I can't believe these words

08:21.800 --> 08:24.090
can get uninterested students
to become involved.

08:24.460 --> 08:25.430
Therefore,

08:25.510 --> 08:27.930
I propose a teacher review process.

08:28.310 --> 08:29.310
By doing so,

08:29.390 --> 08:31.720
we'll be able to create a student council

08:31.810 --> 08:36.140
consisting of truly outstanding students
who are approved by the teachers.

08:36.640 --> 08:38.320
In order to create a student council

08:38.400 --> 08:42.690
with higher proficiency, capability,
dignity, and authority,

08:43.110 --> 08:46.030
please cast your votes in favour.

08:46.780 --> 08:49.330
Thank you for listening.

08:55.160 --> 08:56.130
Next,

08:56.210 --> 08:58.500
let's have the opposition
present their arguments.

08:58.880 --> 08:59.920
Yes.

09:00.960 --> 09:02.500
How's she going to turn the tables?

09:02.590 --> 09:05.130
No, Taniyama
is definitely going to win this.

09:05.460 --> 09:08.010
Let's hear what the solitary princess

09:08.100 --> 09:09.470
has to say.

09:14.010 --> 09:17.730
The coolest version of myself in my mind.

09:21.570 --> 09:22.900
That's right.

09:24.570 --> 09:26.700
I'm Kujou, the student council treasurer.

09:26.950 --> 09:28.830
Regarding this agenda,

09:29.080 --> 09:30.780
as the student council representative,

09:30.870 --> 09:32.830
I'll be the opposition.

09:36.790 --> 09:38.590
Taniyama mentioned earlier

09:38.670 --> 09:41.090
that through a teacher review system,

09:41.170 --> 09:44.000
the student council's
authority will be elevated.

09:44.500 --> 09:45.420
However,

09:45.500 --> 09:47.220
I have the opposite opinion.

09:47.430 --> 09:50.100
In fact, I believe
it will decline instead.

09:50.470 --> 09:51.510
Why is that so?

09:51.600 --> 09:53.220
Because it will deprive core members

09:53.300 --> 09:55.850
of the student council,
the president and vice president,

09:55.930 --> 09:59.230
of the right to appoint executives
of the student council.

10:00.270 --> 10:02.270
Speaking of which, in the student council,

10:02.360 --> 10:05.820
the parties who are most admired
and envied by students

10:05.900 --> 10:09.910
are the president and vice president
who win through an election.

10:10.370 --> 10:12.700
It's precisely because
they win the fierce election

10:12.780 --> 10:15.410
and gain this position

10:15.780 --> 10:19.000
that the school
will give them a lot of power.

10:19.670 --> 10:22.080
The right to appoint
the student council executives

10:22.170 --> 10:24.630
is arguably the most representative
form of authority.

10:25.170 --> 10:29.470
Although we're only handing over
some of the authority to teachers,

10:29.550 --> 10:31.300
is this really appropriate?

10:31.760 --> 10:32.760
Isn't that saying

10:32.840 --> 10:36.300
that the current student council
needs the help of the teachers

10:36.390 --> 10:40.400
to uphold its own dignity?

10:41.270 --> 10:45.020
This school places great importance
on student self-government.

10:45.400 --> 10:48.700
The reason why the student council
is granted tremendous discretion

10:48.780 --> 10:49.990
is also because of this.

10:50.660 --> 10:53.410
If the selection
of student council executives

10:53.490 --> 10:55.280
includes a teacher review process,

10:55.370 --> 10:56.830
what will happen then?

10:57.290 --> 10:59.080
Would the president and vice president

10:59.170 --> 11:01.080
be able to let promising students

11:01.170 --> 11:04.920
join the student council freely?

11:05.460 --> 11:08.130
They also wouldn't be able
to turn down executives

11:08.220 --> 11:10.430
approved by the teachers, right?

11:10.510 --> 11:11.340
Yes.

11:11.430 --> 11:13.090
- She spoke her mind calmly.
- So, this

11:13.180 --> 11:15.430
- Perfect.
- is transferring the right of appointment

11:15.510 --> 11:18.020
- Taniyama's claim and Alya's claim
- to the teachers.

11:18.100 --> 11:20.100
- both have their merits.
- Doesn't that mean

11:20.190 --> 11:23.140
- We're even now.
- the council has veered off course?

11:23.230 --> 11:24.190
Taniyama.

11:24.390 --> 11:26.700
These aren't my ideas,

11:26.780 --> 11:28.700
but Alya's own thoughts.

11:30.070 --> 11:32.820
Thank you for listening.

11:34.360 --> 11:37.040
Now, it's time for questions.

11:37.120 --> 11:38.120
I have a question.

11:39.000 --> 11:40.120
Go ahead.

11:40.870 --> 11:42.960
As I was saying,

11:43.040 --> 11:44.210
in the past few years,

11:44.290 --> 11:47.630
all students who wanted to join
the council have become executives.

11:48.050 --> 11:50.220
As long as there are no problems,

11:50.300 --> 11:52.220
I think it's fine.

11:52.550 --> 11:54.590
To prevent the standards from declining,

11:54.670 --> 11:57.600
I think it's necessary to include
the supervision of teachers.

11:58.230 --> 12:02.810
Shouldn't the student council president
and the vice president decide that?

12:03.060 --> 12:05.480
Admitting that you're not good enough

12:05.570 --> 12:07.490
and seeking help from the teachers

12:07.570 --> 12:09.110
is also a kind of resolution.

12:09.490 --> 12:13.190
But it's not something we can decide.

12:13.990 --> 12:17.330
You failed because you
misjudged your opponent.

12:18.040 --> 12:20.870
Your opponent was Alya from the start.

12:20.950 --> 12:22.910
But you've been watching me.

12:23.790 --> 12:24.700
Next,

12:24.790 --> 12:25.910
what will you do?

12:27.710 --> 12:28.670
Then,

12:28.760 --> 12:32.130
what if the president
and vice president go berserk?

12:32.510 --> 12:33.340
Well...

12:33.420 --> 12:35.920
But Kujou is an outsider after all, right?

12:37.390 --> 12:40.100
What would a transfer student
know about this school?

12:40.180 --> 12:42.100
Taniyama is better, isn't she?

12:43.680 --> 12:45.270
So she pulled this trick?

12:45.810 --> 12:47.020
Are they shills?

12:47.480 --> 12:48.610
What?

12:49.480 --> 12:50.820
Please answer.

12:52.320 --> 12:54.110
What? What did she just say?

12:54.690 --> 12:56.900
Hurry, I have to answer her.

12:57.700 --> 12:59.620
But what should I say?

13:09.670 --> 13:11.300
You did well.

13:11.380 --> 13:12.630
Leave the rest to me.

13:17.260 --> 13:20.010
Sorry for interrupting
in the middle of a question.

13:20.100 --> 13:22.720
I'll take over from here.

13:23.100 --> 13:26.060
Did you lose your voice
from talking for too long?

13:26.140 --> 13:27.230
Come on.

13:27.320 --> 13:29.650
That happened
because you don't usually talk much.

13:32.400 --> 13:33.400
Well then,

13:33.480 --> 13:35.980
for my partner who lost her voice,

13:36.070 --> 13:38.700
I want to end this meeting
as soon as possible.

13:39.160 --> 13:40.490
But ultimately,

13:40.580 --> 13:42.530
is it necessary
to continue this discussion?

13:45.200 --> 13:48.000
The moment you chose
this President Kenzaki,

13:48.090 --> 13:50.920
your feelings were clear, right?

13:52.090 --> 13:54.000
As you all know,

13:54.090 --> 13:55.340
President Kenzaki used to be

13:55.420 --> 13:57.800
an unremarkable,
sub-par student in his class.

13:58.100 --> 13:59.930
I'll take this chance to make it clear.

14:00.010 --> 14:04.510
President Kenzaki was a darned gloomy man
who could never be approved by teachers.

14:06.560 --> 14:07.400
But

14:07.480 --> 14:09.730
President Kenzaki put in a lot of effort.

14:10.060 --> 14:11.190
He improved his grades

14:11.270 --> 14:12.480
and honed his masculinity.

14:12.560 --> 14:16.990
He went from a gloomy loser to a dignified
student council presidential candidate.

14:17.370 --> 14:21.370
You all once supported him, didn't you?

14:23.950 --> 14:26.710
President Kenzaki became
the student council president

14:26.780 --> 14:27.920
because of this system

14:28.000 --> 14:29.250
which allows any student

14:29.330 --> 14:32.630
to become a student council executive
as long as they have passion.

14:33.460 --> 14:35.210
I'll ask again.

14:35.290 --> 14:37.720
Is there really a need
for further discussion?

14:42.840 --> 14:46.600
The sudden tease by my junior
took me by surprise.

14:46.850 --> 14:48.600
But if there are no more questions,

14:48.690 --> 14:50.810
we'll move on to the final debate.

14:50.900 --> 14:52.520
Proposition, do you agree?

14:55.060 --> 14:56.020
What?

14:56.110 --> 14:57.950
Hey, Sayacchi!

14:59.490 --> 15:00.610
Alya!

15:05.780 --> 15:08.710
Okay, we surrender.

15:09.170 --> 15:10.120
What?

15:11.580 --> 15:14.120
In that case,
we will reject the proposition's motion.

15:14.210 --> 15:15.790
Are you okay with that?

15:15.880 --> 15:17.380
Yes, I am.

15:17.720 --> 15:21.430
Oh, dear. My Sayaka has disturbed you.

15:23.970 --> 15:26.220
Well then, the motion is rejected.

15:26.770 --> 15:28.940
That concludes the general meeting.

15:29.020 --> 15:30.020
What?

15:33.270 --> 15:36.310
I'm counting on you, Masachika.

15:36.390 --> 15:38.780
Right, leave it to me, Yuki.

15:39.900 --> 15:41.610
When I saw those two,

15:41.990 --> 15:44.110
I thought they were the ideal ones.

15:44.990 --> 15:48.660
A relationship where they completely trust
one another and have each other's backs.

15:50.660 --> 15:54.250
Those two had a deep bond
that no one could match.

15:55.080 --> 15:57.800
It was inevitable
that I couldn't beat them.

15:58.670 --> 16:00.840
While I was a little envious, this made me

16:00.920 --> 16:02.800
finally give up competing against them.

16:04.590 --> 16:05.590
That's why

16:06.130 --> 16:08.020
when I saw those two,

16:11.640 --> 16:13.520
I felt betrayed.

16:18.400 --> 16:19.530
Wait!

16:26.110 --> 16:27.000
Why?

16:27.080 --> 16:28.700
Why is it you?

16:28.790 --> 16:30.160
Kuze and Suou

16:30.250 --> 16:32.540
are one-of-a-kind partners.

16:32.620 --> 16:33.750
It's because of them

16:33.870 --> 16:34.790
that I...

16:35.620 --> 16:38.800
That I... gave up.

16:39.800 --> 16:40.920
Why?

16:47.560 --> 16:49.560
If you have something to say to me,

16:49.640 --> 16:51.310
just let it all out.

16:52.930 --> 16:56.310
I have no right to say anything to you.

16:57.430 --> 16:59.610
I'm such an idiot.

17:00.480 --> 17:01.900
I believed on my own,

17:01.980 --> 17:03.110
admired on my own,

17:03.400 --> 17:05.320
and felt betrayed on my own.

17:05.400 --> 17:06.440
I even threw a tantrum.

17:08.740 --> 17:12.120
Clearly, it was all my self-conceit.

17:16.490 --> 17:18.090
There you are.

17:20.670 --> 17:22.800
She's crying so much.

17:23.250 --> 17:24.920
I'm sorry, Kujou.

17:25.170 --> 17:28.180
Leave this to me.

17:28.470 --> 17:29.310
Well...

17:29.390 --> 17:31.010
It's fine.

17:31.100 --> 17:32.430
Okay? Please.

17:36.310 --> 17:37.520
Taniyama.

17:37.610 --> 17:40.400
Actually, I also don't know

17:40.480 --> 17:43.190
why Kuze chose me.

17:43.570 --> 17:44.690
But

17:44.770 --> 17:47.330
I want to live up to his expectations.

17:48.160 --> 17:49.990
So I'll do my best.

17:50.160 --> 17:53.330
I'll make you acknowledge me someday.

17:53.870 --> 17:55.120
That's all.

17:57.840 --> 18:01.250
Oh dear, Kujou is such a good girl.

18:01.340 --> 18:02.790
Yes.

18:03.290 --> 18:05.500
After all, she's the one chosen by Kuze.

18:05.880 --> 18:07.050
Once you've calmed down,

18:07.130 --> 18:10.010
you can then apologize
to Kuzecchi and Kujou.

18:10.260 --> 18:12.100
I'll go with you.

18:17.560 --> 18:19.690
My brother is still too naive.

18:20.060 --> 18:21.860
If he really wanted to,

18:21.940 --> 18:24.810
he could have ended this farce right away.

18:25.360 --> 18:26.690
Well, it doesn't matter.

18:26.780 --> 18:28.200
If that's all it takes,

18:28.280 --> 18:30.530
they aren't my enemies after all.

18:30.780 --> 18:31.990
And that naivety

18:32.070 --> 18:34.530
will lead them to self-destruction
in the near future.

18:34.950 --> 18:36.580
Don't you think so?

18:36.660 --> 18:38.040
Is that so?

18:38.380 --> 18:40.210
I think Master Masachika
and Mistress Alisa

18:40.290 --> 18:42.500
are extraordinary.

18:44.170 --> 18:45.290
Ayano.

18:45.380 --> 18:46.340
Yes?

18:46.760 --> 18:47.840
You don't understand.

18:47.930 --> 18:49.430
You really don't get it.

18:49.510 --> 18:50.930
Be absolutely fearless,

18:51.010 --> 18:52.010
have full control,

18:52.090 --> 18:53.340
darken your eye corners,

18:53.510 --> 18:56.180
and finally, act all high and mighty
while judging others.

18:56.270 --> 19:00.350
These are the keys to creating
the vibes of a strong opponent!

19:01.480 --> 19:02.980
I'm really sorry.

19:03.060 --> 19:05.020
I didn't know better.

19:05.690 --> 19:08.610
Come on, get it together.

19:09.070 --> 19:13.700
Why do you think I accepted
this freaking hot lighting job?

19:14.230 --> 19:15.070
(Loyalty, Righteousness)

19:16.990 --> 19:18.420
Forgive my presumption,

19:18.500 --> 19:20.210
but may I ask you something?

19:20.290 --> 19:21.580
What is it?

19:21.670 --> 19:24.000
You mentioned creating
the vibes of a strong opponent.

19:24.080 --> 19:28.220
Isn't that what the final loser does?

19:30.550 --> 19:31.380
Also,

19:31.470 --> 19:33.220
as I reminded you earlier,

19:33.300 --> 19:35.630
no eating or drinking
in the lighting control room.

19:37.180 --> 19:39.520
Ayano, clean this up.

19:39.980 --> 19:41.310
As you wish.

19:44.560 --> 19:46.610
Taniyama said

19:47.070 --> 19:49.700
that she thought
you and Yuki were a unique pair.

19:49.780 --> 19:51.200
She admired you two a lot.

19:51.570 --> 19:53.610
That's why she gave up on the election.

19:53.990 --> 19:54.990
I see.

19:55.870 --> 19:57.910
I'll do my best.

19:58.870 --> 20:01.910
I'll make Taniyama admit someday

20:02.000 --> 20:03.870
that you didn't make a mistake

20:04.210 --> 20:07.300
by choosing to run with me.

20:08.090 --> 20:10.920
You're right. I'll do my best too.

20:12.130 --> 20:14.380
Hey, can I ask you something?

20:15.550 --> 20:17.390
Why did you choose

20:17.470 --> 20:20.270
to run with me instead of Yuki?

20:22.560 --> 20:25.390
The reason I led the student council
with Yuki back then

20:25.640 --> 20:28.690
was because I couldn't refuse her request.

20:29.780 --> 20:33.820
I did want to support her
in achieving her goal,

20:34.570 --> 20:36.030
but I think the main reason

20:36.400 --> 20:38.700
was that I felt guilty.

20:39.200 --> 20:40.500
Guilty?

20:46.960 --> 20:48.420
Maybe that's why

20:48.670 --> 20:51.130
I always felt suffocated.

20:51.590 --> 20:53.420
Compared to the people around me

20:53.510 --> 20:57.100
who worked so hard
for their dreams and goals,

20:57.390 --> 21:00.720
my motivation was pathetic.

21:00.970 --> 21:03.810
At that time,
I often thought about self-abuse.

21:04.770 --> 21:07.940
Everyone called me
"Vice President in the Shadows",

21:08.570 --> 21:10.190
but in the end,

21:10.280 --> 21:13.110
I just didn't want to be in the spotlight.

21:16.030 --> 21:16.990
But

21:17.080 --> 21:18.540
it's different this time.

21:18.990 --> 21:20.120
With my own free will,

21:20.200 --> 21:22.450
I decided to run for vice president

21:23.040 --> 21:24.620
because I want to work hard...

21:24.700 --> 21:25.620
together with you.

21:30.250 --> 21:31.710
So, well,

21:31.960 --> 21:34.130
you don't have
to compare yourself to Yuki.

21:34.550 --> 21:35.840
How should I put it?

21:36.210 --> 21:37.680
Well, you know...

21:37.760 --> 21:39.310
It's something along that line.

21:40.390 --> 21:41.810
About this,

21:41.890 --> 21:43.810
I wish you'd be more specific.

21:44.260 --> 21:45.220
Shut up.

21:45.310 --> 21:46.680
Are you making fun of me?

21:46.770 --> 21:47.900
I'm not telling you.

21:48.270 --> 21:50.400
By the way, what about you?

21:50.480 --> 21:51.520
What do you mean?

21:51.900 --> 21:54.480
Why do you want to run with me?

21:54.820 --> 21:57.120
Oh my, it's simple.

21:59.580 --> 22:01.620
[Because it's you.]

22:04.950 --> 22:06.700
What does that mean?

22:13.420 --> 22:15.420
It's time to go home.

22:19.010 --> 22:20.300
All right.

22:20.970 --> 22:22.510
By the way, Kuze,

22:22.600 --> 22:24.050
what was that just now?

22:24.140 --> 22:25.180
Just now?

22:25.760 --> 22:28.400
Something about the size of my boobs.

22:28.480 --> 22:30.650
Oh, that?

22:30.730 --> 22:32.110
Well,

22:32.190 --> 22:35.150
a girl I know brought it up.

22:35.650 --> 22:39.780
And then, the person said
that you should be an E cup.

22:41.030 --> 22:42.700
Barely right.

22:45.660 --> 22:46.620
What?

22:47.160 --> 22:48.210
Barely?
